#### Stance Details (SOUL Tier — 441 Round Decisions)

1. **`D` Stance — Neutral Control (56.9% / 251 Decisions):**
* **`D+L` (Combo Punch / Poke):** 138 uses (55.0% of pokes) — Primary low-risk neutral positioning action.
* **`D+J` (Standard Jab):** 58 uses — High-priority initiative setup.
* **`D+K` (Low Sweep):** 40 uses — Spacing and state reset.
* **`D+I` (Rider Whip Poke):** 15 uses — Mid-range Chi resource generator.


2. **`S` Stance — High-Value Action Conversions (34.5% / 152 Decisions):**
* **`S+J` (Rider Chop / Kick):** **115 uses (75.7% of all specials)** — Core execution choice for exploiting opponent high-cost stance commitments.
* **`S+I` (Kirimomi Kick):** 25 uses — High-cost heavy damage conversion.
* **`S+L` (Rider Kick):** 9 uses.
* **`S+K` (X-Chop variant):** 3 uses.


3. **`A` Stance — Defensive Omni Guard (3.4% / 15 Decisions):**
* **`A+I` (Windmill Omni Guard):** **14 uses (93.3% of all guards)**.
* **`A+J` (High Block):** 1 use.


4. **`W` Stance — Utility & LP Sustain (2.0% / 9 Decisions):**
* **`W+L` (Kaizorg Vitality Recovery):** 7 uses — Tactical healing during distance resets.
* **`W+K` (Utility stance):** 2 uses.



---

### 4. Key Tactical & Engine Insights

#### 1. `A+I` Windmill Guard Optimization (93.3% Guard Share)

Under the updated Guard Chi-reward system ($\lfloor 0.5 \times \text{chiCost} \rfloor + 1$), blocking an opponent's 3-Chi Windmill or 6-Chi Special returns **+2 to +4 Chi**. The retrained Q-weights correctly treat `A+I` as a net Chi generator, allowing `RIDER` live search to deploy `A+I` during opponent attack setups for optimal resource conversion.

#### 2. Adaptive Policy Scaling

* **Low-Tier Suppression (Easy / Balanced):** The direct matrix allocates **> 52% of actions into `S` stance specials**, overpowering low-lookahead opponent decision logic in ~12.7 rounds.
* **High-Tier Calculation (SOUL):** Under deep search, the model shifts **56.9% of turns into `D` stance neutral pokes**, storing Chi for 115 `S+J` value executions and 7 `W+L` vitality casts.

