#### Granular Action Selection by Tier

##### A. Direct Execution Tiers (Random & Easy — High Pace Offensive Focus)

* **`S` Stance (Specials — ~40% share):** Direct neural execution against low-lookahead opponents skips defensive setups and dumps meter straight into **`S+J` (Rider Chop — 428 uses vs Random / 293 uses vs Easy)** and **`S+K` (142 vs Random / 87 vs Easy)**.
* **`D` Stance (Pokes — ~36% share):** Neutral control is driven primarily by **`D+I` (Rider Whip Poke — 292 uses vs Random)** and **`D+L` (Combo Punch — 180 uses vs Easy)**.
* **`A` Stance (Guards — 15–17% share):** High volume of defensive selections (`A+J` high guard and `A+I` Windmill) to absorb loose random actions.

##### B. Search Execution Tiers (Balanced, Master & SOUL — Attrition & Control)

* **`D` Stance (Neutral Poking — 49.3% to 67.9% share):** Against deep opponent lookahead, RIDER pivots away from direct special selection and locks down state space with **`D+L` (Combo Punch)** and **`D+J` (Standard Jab)**.
* **`S` Stance (Special Conversions — 13.5% to 24.6% share):** Specials are strictly reserved for high-probability value conversion steps, with **`S+J` (Rider Chop)** accounting for **79.6% of all special decisions** across Master and SOUL settings (51 out of 64 in SOUL; 23 out of 33 in Master).
* **`A` Stance (Omni Guard — 3.7% to 7.4% share):** Out of all defensive actions executed under search, **`A+I` (Windmill Omni Guard)** accounts for **88.2% to 95.8% of guards** (17 out of 20 in SOUL; 23 out of 24 in Balanced), exploiting the Chi refund rules.
* **`W` Stance (Utility & Healing — 3.0% to 12.5% share):** High-tier SOUL matches demand active health management, logging **18 `W+K` utility steps** and **16 `W+L` Kaizorg Vitality recovery casts (+250 LP each)** to out-sustain V3 across 26.3 rounds.

---

### 4. Combat Style & Archetype Analysis: Ichigo vs. V3

```
[ V3 High Offense / Specials ] ──> [ A+I Windmill Omni Guard ] ──> [ +4 to +6 Chi Refund ]
                                                                             │
[ Win (60% SOUL / 80% Master) ] <── [ W+L Healing & S+J Execution ] <─── [ Neutral Meter Bank ]

```

#### 1. Archetype Dynamics (High-Sustain Heavy vs. High-Resource Striker)

Kamen Rider V3 possesses high mobility and high-cost special routines. When Ichigo attempts pure direct policy stance selection against V3's high tiers, V3's lookahead out-evaluates direct policy stance choices. However, when paired with **RIDER live search**, Ichigo shifts into a **High-Sustain Attrition Decision Engine**:

* **Neutral Phase:** Ichigo uses low-commitment `D+L` pokes to bait V3 into throwing high-cost specials.
* **Defensive Phase:** When V3 commits to high-cost specials, RIDER triggers `A+I` Windmill Omni Guard. Under the updated guard rule ($\lfloor 0.5 \times \text{chiCost} \rfloor + 1$), blocking V3's 6-Chi or 10-Chi attacks nets Ichigo **+1 to +3 profit in Chi**.
* **Value Conversion & Sustain Phase:** Stored Chi is split between **`W+L` Kaizorg Vitality (+250 LP recovery)** to erase V3's chip damage and **`S+J` (Rider Chop)** to exploit V3's post-special state commitments.

#### 2. Dual-Policy Scaling Profile

* **Low-Tier Mode (`network` policy):** Fast, aggressive, special-heavy (16.2 rounds avg duration; 41.2% special share). Optimal for rapid processing against unoptimized opponents.
* **High-Tier Mode (`rider` search policy):** Patient, defensive, high-sustain attrition (26.3 to 28.4 rounds avg duration; 12.5% healing share; 88.2%+ `A+I` guard share). Built specifically to disarm deep search AI.

