* **`D+L` (Combo Punch / Mid Poke):** Dominates high-tier search lookahead (**38 uses / 61.3% of pokes in Master**; **38 uses in SOUL**). Intercepts Ichigo's heavy forward initiative before defensive priority triggers.
* **`D+K` (Low Sweep):** Heavily utilized in direct neural mode (**234 uses in Easy**) to force state resets.
* **`D+I` (Range Poke):** Consistent mid-range Chi generator across all tiers (17 uses in Master, 15 in Balanced, 184 in Easy).


2. **Special Action Conversion Engine (`S` Stance — 34.1% to 42.7% Share):**
* **`S+K` (Violent Slash / Jaguar Shock):** Core finisher choice across all tree-search tiers (**30 uses / 58.8% of specials in Master**; **30 in Balanced**; **36 in SOUL**).
* **`S+J` (Rider Kick / Secondary Special):** Secondary value conversion choice (10 uses in Master, 109 in Easy).


3. **High-Tier Mobility Management (`W` Stance — 7.2% to 8.5% Share):**
* Under Master and SOUL lookahead, `ForeseeEngine` incorporates **`W+I` range leap positioning** (9 out of 11 utility decisions in Master) to shift out of Ichigo's linear action vectors rather than taking block damage.


4. **Defensive Economy (`A` Stance — 0.0% to 3.4% Share):**
* Amazon's policy relies almost entirely on range spacing and interrupt pokes, keeping guard allocation under 3.5% across all settings.



